<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		Self-signed profile — INTERNAL builds only.

		Selected by afterPack.js when the signing identity is not a
		"Developer ID Application: …" certificate. The public,
		notarized profile is entitlements.mac.plist and deliberately
		omits the two relaxations below.

		Hardened runtime + self-signed Team ID workaround.

		When the app is signed with a self-signed certificate (i.e. any
		certificate that does NOT come from a paid Apple Developer ID
		program), the TeamIdentifier field in every signature is empty.
		dyld4 on macOS 13+ enforces library validation under the
		hardened runtime and rejects cross-image loads whenever the
		consuming process and the loaded framework do not share a
		non-empty Team ID — treating two different "empty" Team IDs as
		distinct. That is what produces:

		    mapping process and mapped file (non-platform) have
		    different Team IDs

		at launch, even though Transcriptor.app and Electron Framework
		are both signed by the same self-signed certificate.

		The official Apple-sanctioned way to opt out of library
		validation is the com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-
		validation entitlement. It is specifically designed for cases
		where the main binary legitimately loads plug-ins or
		frameworks that were signed by a different identity — which is
		exactly our situation with self-signed code. Electron's own
		documentation recommends this entitlement when shipping
		outside a notarized Developer ID workflow.

		afterPack.js passes this file to Transcriptor.app and
		entitlements.mac.selfsigned.inherit.plist to nested helpers,
		frameworks and the bundled Python runtime, because each helper
		also loads Electron Framework under the same hardened-runtime
		library-validation path.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
